cff-version: 1.2.0
message: |-
  If you use stataskills in academic work, please cite both this skill
  collection and the underlying textbook (see `references` below).
type: software
title: "stataskills: 10 Stata Skills distilled from A Gentle Introduction to Stata (6th edition)"
abstract: |-
  Ten Agent skills — four (stata-basics, stata-descriptives, stata-regression,
  stata-advanced) that distill Alan C. Acock's "A Gentle Introduction to
  Stata" (6th edition), plus six extensions covering coefficient plots,
  official and community difference-in-differences methods, regression
  discontinuity, selection on observables, and identification design routing
  — callable from Claude Code, Codex, OpenClaw and other skill-compatible
  runtimes. Each skill ships with command guidance, interpretation logic,
  reporting conventions, and a pitfalls checklist, plus the 38 .dta AGIS6
  datasets and governed project-level extension datasets used by verification.
version: 0.1.0
